 "about_text": "Talion Gallery is a contemporary art gallery in Tokyo, founded in Yanaka in 2011 and relocated to Mejiro in 2014. Its name references the ancient principle of retributive justice, 'an eye for an eye,' reflecting the gallery's stated aim of generating new connections among the people, institutions, language and money that shape the contemporary art world. The gallery represents a small roster of Japanese artists working across painting, drawing, video and installation, and has participated in international art fairs including Art Düsseldorf, ART OSAKA, Art Fair Tokyo and the Seattle Art Fair, alongside museum and project-space collaborations in Japan and abroad.",
